The behavior you're seeing — useEffect firing on every render despite a dependency array — points to one of a few specific cases. Here are the most common ones, with fixes:

1. **Dependency array is empty but function is re-created each render**:
```jsx
function MyComponent() {
  const handleClick = () => { /* ... */ }

  useEffect(() => {
    // This runs every render because handleClick is a new function each time
    // even if the dependency array is [], the function argument is new
  }, [handleClick])

  return <button onClick={handleClick}>Click</button>
}
```
**Fix**: Use useCallback to memoize the function:
```jsx
const handleClick = useCallback(() => { /* ... */ }, [])

useEffect(() => {
  // Now this runs only when the dependency changes, not on every render
}, [handleClick])
```

2. **Object or array dependency is re-created on every render**:
```jsx
const searchParams = { page: 1, limit: 10 }
useEffect(() => {
  fetch('/api', searchParams) // This runs every render because searchParams is new each time
}, [searchParams])
```
